-- if-and-or
insert into public.items (slug, kind, title, summary, owner_id, stored_at, duration_seconds, origin, source) values ('if-and-or', 'video', 'If And Or', 'Walks through using the IF, AND, and OR functions together to model
cash flows that start and end in specific years, including how to
lock cell references correctly.', (select id from public.owners where slug = 'not-established'), 'https://player.vimeo.com/video/1192297394?dnt=1', 370, 'primitive', 'myrumbo:excel-for-finance (WhisperX transcript, Vimeo upload)');
insert into public.items (slug, kind, title, summary, owner_id, body_md, origin, derived_from, source) values ('if-and-or--read', 'read', 'If And Or: reading', 'Walks through using the IF, AND, and OR functions together to model
cash flows that start and end in specific years, including how to
lock cell references correctly.', (select id from public.owners where slug = 'not-established'), '## IF, AND, and OR in a cash flow model

The IF function takes three arguments: a logical test, the value to
return if the test is true, and the value to return if it is false.
To model cash flows that only appear from year three onward, the
logical test checks whether the year cell is greater than or equal
to a start year input. Lock the start year cell with F4 ($D$3) so
it stays fixed when you copy the formula down.

Lock every input cell reference — discount rates, start years, cash
flow amounts — with F4. A common mistake is referencing the cash flow
cell without locking it, causing the formula to drift to the wrong
row as you copy it down.

## Combining IF with AND

To add an end year, wrap the logical test inside an AND function.
AND returns true only when every condition inside it is true. The
formula becomes: IF(AND(year >= start, year <= end), cash_flow, 0).
This restricts cash flows to a specific window of years.

When editing inside the formula bar, you cannot use arrow keys to
navigate to other cells — Excel will move the formula cursor instead.
Either type the cell address directly or click the target cell with
the mouse.

## Switching to OR

OR returns true if any one of its conditions is true. Replacing AND
with OR in the same formula means cash flows appear whenever the year
is either greater than the start or less than the end — which covers
almost every period. Understanding this difference lets you build
models that respond dynamically to changing inputs.', 'derived', (select id from public.items where slug = 'if-and-or'), 'myrumbo descriptor prompt (read_content)');
